* The fundamental theorem of calculus through an affine substitution: if ` A ( y ) ` has the continuous derivative ` B ( y ) ` on ` RR+ ` and ` K t + H > 0 ` on ` [ P , Q ] ` , then ` S. ( P , Q ) B ( K t + H ) _d t = ( A ( K Q + H ) - A ( K P + H ) ) / K ` ( ~ ef1ftc , ~ dvmptco , ~ cncfcompt2 ).  Both interval helpers of ExplicitFormula are instances.

